// ── 10.7 / 10.8
labour: [
["10.7","Ethical labour, in the factory as well as on the site","This clause applies to the Contractor, to every sub-contractor and to the place of manufacture, wherever in the world that is. It is written because this package is a manufacturing package as much as a construction package, and a modern slavery policy that stops at the site gate does not reach the people who build the modules.\n\nThe Contractor shall comply with the Modern Slavery Act 2015 and shall publish a statement under section 54 where its turnover requires it; where it does not, it shall provide an equivalent policy. In addition, and in respect of every person working on this package including in the factory: no worker shall pay any fee to obtain or keep employment, and any such fee already paid shall be reimbursed — the Employer Pays Principle applies without exception; no worker's passport or identity document shall be retained by any party; every worker shall have a written contract in a language they understand, stating pay, hours and the notice required to leave; no worker shall be prevented from leaving employment or from leaving accommodation provided with it; and working time records shall be kept and made available.\n\nWhere the factory provides or arranges accommodation for its workforce, that accommodation shall meet a recognised standard for worker accommodation and shall be disclosed. The Employer notes the position it would be in if the modules for a workers' accommodation village were built by people in unacceptable accommodation, and does not intend to be in it.\n\nDISCLOSURE AND AUDIT. The Contractor shall disclose, with its tender, the location of every place at which the modules and the principal fit-out components will be manufactured. The Employer may audit any of them on reasonable notice, may bring an independent auditor, and may interview workers privately and without a representative of the Contractor present. A place of manufacture not disclosed at tender shall not be used without the Employer's written agreement. Refusal of access is a breach."],
["10.8","Occupational health","The Contractor shall assess and control, for its own workforce and in its method statements: manual handling of module components and fit-out items; hand-arm vibration; noise, both its own and that of the adjoining construction site; respirable crystalline silica and wood dust in the factory; and work at height during setting and connection. Health surveillance shall be provided where the assessment requires it, and the Contractor shall confirm at tender that it is in place rather than that it will be arranged."],
],

